7592186167588}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166756 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166594 :question/id #uuid "d5eeb5a1-4bfd-5f1e-b261-548c91eec64b" :question/math-academy-id "e-8339"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1979b91d-2ac0-5d35-b4cc-1c9c9505b503" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167335} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167353} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360604} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516767} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516800} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516844} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518156} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518178} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534976} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535042}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Tanh Function"} :step/id #uuid "ef9c2df4-390a-50bb-8e1e-90ff592b4bee" :step/math-academy-id 31146 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167589}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166757 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166595 :question/id #uuid "7cd3958b-aa1c-5c9a-b2ef-a21002aa7ff1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8340"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57d851ce-44b5-5713-ba65-7f5a9cc1122f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048813} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048842}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167336} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167337} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518158} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518214} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535003}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"} :step/id #uuid "80771e82-bccd-5a3a-b98a-e59fd31c7940" :step/math-academy-id 31147 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167710}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167701 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168091 :tutorial/content "The derivatives of the base inverse hyperbolic functions are shown below:\n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}, &  & \\,x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}, &  & \\,x\\in (1,\\infty ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x) & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}, &  & \\,x\\in (-1,1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we know the derivative of the base inverse hyperbolic functions, we can differentiate combinations of these functions, by using the properties of differentiation.\n\nFor example, let's find the derivative of \n\n$$\ny = \\arcosh(x^2).\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡({x}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{({x}^{2})^{2}-1}}\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "30ebb598-5737-5a10-9f96-b450c6c56039" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5209 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9c01d83c-633c-5a68-bac0-26e7193c94c5" :step/math-academy-id 32693 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167586}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167710 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168100 :tutorial/content "We derive formulas for the derivatives of the inverse hyperbolic functions from the functions' definitions. \n$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFor instance, let's show that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsinh{x}) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^2+1}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that\n\n$$\n\\arsinh{x} = \\ln\\big(x+\\sqrt{x^2+1}\\big).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating using the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1})) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot (x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1+\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}})}{x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}+x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1})} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}\\cancel{(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we can obtain the other formulas." :tutorial/id #uuid "05e38300-7cf8-5c4d-b35e-139ea77d72ee" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5225 :tutorial/title "Deriving the Derivatives of Inverse Hyperbolic Functions"} :step/id #uuid "10ef08f5-4066-5fac-874a-baef7c0c14e5" :step/math-academy-id 32715}] :activity/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186167019}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535143} :activity/id #uuid "fe9eb0bd-24ad-5960-8681-02004f47daf0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049314 :topic/id #uuid "eb87a0b0-198f-5c1c-98ee-ceab471e0302" :topic/math-academy-id 3252} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535099 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3ea6a3a-8078-5e78-9e2e-c7ecb759b2d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{1-3x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534808}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534808} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cde32a2-c89a-582c-93af-924f59b3619d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "973108cd-4a12-5f7e-8def-c33e7591ffaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-342458" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\sqrt{7}\\,\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)) \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{3}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{7}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-3{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3{x}^{2}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "20ca1f8e-33d8-5d92-9a68-9b271fbbb6eb" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535106}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535106 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534976 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2bbc451-3971-5718-9b6a-c792cbf3baa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1-{x}^{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534768}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534768} :answer-field/id #uuid "caf30c59-3266-50ba-a4bd-cf968c8851d8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0bc32c07-1675-5c17-a61b-a851fe6dbaf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342471" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $5{x}^{4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{5})}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{5})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{10}}\\cdot 5{x}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{4}}{1-{x}^{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "39fef160-1d58-52ed-94e8-3b82d441f7ea" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535109}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535109 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86653cab-377d-5ed8-a471-e37ef1bae183" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+(4x+3)^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534555}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534555} :answer-field/id #uuid "958fb880-28de-5a44-b1da-b802306a2223" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "40534571-9b68-5a71-b2eb-96fad07c5254" :question/math-academy-id "q-342666" :question/problem "$$\n\nCalculate ${g}^{′}(x)$ for $g(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3).$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)\\,+$ | $4{e}^{x}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAnd the product rule is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}(u\\cdot v)}{\\text{d}x}={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, chain rule, and  formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & ={({e}^{x})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3))}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4x+3)}^{′} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\,\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡(4x+3)+\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{(4x+3)^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "670e1922-ccd4-5f3d-9789-2c3188ece2f5"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535131 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33841734-1cb4-596a-90ad-9968f0fc8c0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534363} :answer-field/id #uuid "114d9c4c-5ec1-5cf1-a611-dbc9b12d3763" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "727d2976-e027-5f8e-a059-0575427eb806" :question/math-academy-id "q-341959" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(3x-4),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(4\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(3x-4)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(3x-4)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3x-4)^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{(3x-4)^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "cefc5e76-e5ef-5be3-aef8-c08aca913b13" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535099}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535143 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535089 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37c7d91d-cc06-508e-8136-0c7783921fdf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-2)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534372} {:answer/id #uuid "813bb0df-60a0-5317-aae6-74937157ce77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534545} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba4ffdb-ed17-5ed7-ac4b-60e5e8212467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534610} {:answer/id #uuid "b515d758-ad04-57d6-957e-d01e00b0efbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x(2x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534669} {:answer/id #uuid "ece0ec44-e760-591f-b411-d7660b6288df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(2x-1)}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534790}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186534610} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d51b538-39cd-589a-b246-54b69d35dae4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534837}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fd040bd9-e3ef-5708-a352-cc4c61514e23" :question/math-academy-id "q-96426" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡(2x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x-1)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (2x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(4{x}^{2}-4x+1)-1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}-4x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x(x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x(x-1)}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f9309d58-72f3-5655-bced-f00af4482162" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535131}}] :activity/title "Differentiating Inverse Hyperbolic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534266}]}
